{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>ועד הם עומדים יגיפו הדלתות ואחוזו</b> — Scripture in our language sometimes speaks of what is present as though it were hidden from us, as in: \"Let him kiss me with the kisses of his mouth.\"" "<b>והם עומדים</b> — a hint to Hanani and Hananiah. The meaning: while they are standing at the gates, he warned them to shut the gates, close the doors before them. And he said to them: you, grip the doors with the bars." "<b>יגיפו</b> — Targum [of] וסגרת הדלת, and ותגיפין דשא." "<b>והעמד</b> — verb [form]."], :book :nehemiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Nehemiah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/nechemya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:15:26.526222767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}